<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — Exit / Cancel / Shutdown countdown dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual + behavioral PARITY reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormSaveOrNot`
    (source: FormSaveOrNot.cs + FormSaveOrNot.Designer.cs + FormSaveOrNot.resx). Per AAP §0.3.3
    this is a faithful re-platform of the currently rendered Windows Forms surface — never a
    redesign: every size, position and font below is taken verbatim from FormSaveOrNot.Designer.cs.

    The dialog is shown when the operator requests application exit. It offers three mutually
    related choices and shows a live one-second countdown that auto-confirms the active choice:
      * Exit  (btnOk)       — return to Windows / close AgOpenGPS.
      * Cancel (btnReturn)  — abandon the exit and return to AgOpenGPS.
      * Shutdown (btnShutDown) — power off the computer.

    CODE-BEHIND CONTRACT — FormSaveOrNotView.axaml.cs (partial class AgOpenGPS.Views.FormSaveOrNotView : Window):
      * This view is IMPERATIVE, not MVVM: there is intentionally NO x:DataType, no DataContext and
        no {Binding}. All label text and visibility are assigned in code-behind through the x:Name'd
        controls below — exactly mirroring the WinForms ctor + FormSaveOrNot_Load. The x:Name values
        are therefore the integration contract and MUST stay byte-identical to the originals:
            lblQuestion  label2  panel1
            labelShutdown  btnShutDown
            labelCancel    btnReturn
            labelExit      btnOk
            labelShutdownIn  lblShutCtr
            labelExitToWindows  lblExitCtr
      * Caption text is set at runtime from gStr (gsExit / gsShutdown / gsCancel / gsExitToWindows+":" /
        gsShutdownIn+":"); the strings below are the Designer placeholders the code-behind overrides.
      * Visibility: the Exit pair (labelExitToWindows + lblExitCtr) and the Shutdown pair
        (labelShutdownIn + lblShutCtr) are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE. FormSaveOrNot_Load shows exactly one,
        keyed on Settings.setWindow_isShutdownComputer. The defaults below match that setting's
        default (false ⇒ Exit pair visible, Shutdown pair collapsed); the code-behind re-sets all four
        authoritatively when the window loads, so this is only the first-paint state.
      * The three Click handlers (btnOk_Click / btnReturn_Click / btnShutDown_Click) keep the original
        method names. In WinForms the event WIRING lived in the Designer (which this .axaml replaces),
        while the handler bodies live in FormSaveOrNot.cs (which the .axaml.cs replaces) — so wiring the
        clicks here in markup is the faithful division of responsibility.
      * The WinForms System.Windows.Forms.Timer (timer1, 1000 ms) is non-visual and has no XAML element;
        the code-behind reproduces it with a DispatcherTimer (counters start 4 = exit, 5 = shutdown).

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormSaveOrNot.Designer.cs:
      ClientSize 825 x 279        -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" ⇒ client == window)
      FormBorderStyle.None        -> SystemDecorations="None"
      ControlBox = false          -> (no system buttons; implied by SystemDecorations="None")
      (fixed, no min/max)         -> CanResize="False"
      ShowInTaskbar = false       -> ShowInTaskbar="False"
      StartPosition.CenterParent  -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (replaces the WinForms
                                     ScreenHelper.IsOnScreen reposition logic — deliberately NOT ported)
      Padding(5)                  -> Padding="0": WinForms absolutely-positioned children ignore the
                                     form Padding, so applying it would shift every coordinate by 5px
                                     and break pixel parity. The 5px frame had no visual effect here.
      Font Tahoma 8.25            -> FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="11"  (points × 96/72 = device px)

    THEME — unlike the fixed-colour alert dialogs (FormYes / FormSaving / FormDialog), FormSaveOrNot
    used the neutral LightCyan form / AliceBlue panel chrome, so per the assigned spec it tracks the
    app day/night palette: Background = AogFrameBrush and text = AogTextBrush, pulled from the
    App.axaml ThemeDictionaries via {DynamicResource} so the Light<->Dark switch is observed live.
    No WinForms / System.Drawing colours are hard-coded. The near-identical AliceBlue panel is
    represented structurally (panel1 is a transparent grouping Border; the themed window frame shows
    through), preserving the look while remaining theme-aware.

    Font sizes (WinForms points × 96/72 = Avalonia device-independent pixels):
      Tahoma 8.25  -> 11   (form default)
      Tahoma 12    -> 16   (caption labels: Shutdown / Cancel / Exit)
      Tahoma 15.75 -> 21   ("Shutdown In:" / "Exit To Windows In:"; also lblQuestion / label2)
      Tahoma 36    -> 48   (countdown numbers lblShutCtr / lblExitCtr)

    Button glyphs are served from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs,
    mapped from the Designer's BackgroundImage assignments (BackgroundImageLayout.Zoom ⇒ Stretch="Uniform"):
      btnShutDown.BackgroundImage = Resources.SwitchOff    -> btnImages/SwitchOff.png
      btnReturn.BackgroundImage   = Resources.back_button  -> btnImages/back-button.png
      btnOk.BackgroundImage       = Resources.WindowClose  -> btnImages/WindowClose.png

    No WinForms, no System.Drawing, no OpenTK namespaces are referenced — Avalonia 11.3 markup only.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormSaveOrNotView"
        Title="FormSaveOrNot"
        Width="825"
        Height="279"
        CanResize="False"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        Padding="0"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}"
        Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="11">

    <!--
        Flat, chrome-less image buttons reproduce the WinForms FlatStyle.Flat +
        FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + BackColor = Transparent: just the scaled glyph, with no
        button surface in any visual state. The :pointerover / :pressed template overrides suppress
        the Fluent hover/press background that would otherwise box the glyph. Content alignment is
        stretched so the child Image fills the button rectangle and Stretch="Uniform" then scales the
        bitmap to fit while preserving aspect — the exact behaviour of BackgroundImageLayout.Zoom.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Root Canvas == the WinForms client area (825 x 279). The form's three direct children
        (lblQuestion, label2 and panel1) are placed at their exact WinForms client coordinates via
        Canvas.Left / Canvas.Top. Absolute positioning is appropriate because the window is a fixed,
        non-resizable dialog (CanResize="False"), giving true pixel parity with the original.
    -->
    <Canvas>

        <!-- lblQuestion: WinForms Label @ (85,113), Tahoma 15.75 regular, AutoSize. Empty by default
             (the designer set no text and the code-behind leaves it blank); kept for 1:1 control
             parity and so the code-behind can address it by name. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblQuestion"
                   Canvas.Left="85"
                   Canvas.Top="113"
                   FontSize="21"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                   Text="" />

        <!-- label2: WinForms Label @ (487,-28), Tahoma 15.75 regular, AutoSize. Vestigial — empty and
             positioned above the client top in the original, so it has no visual effect. Reproduced
             at its exact (negative) coordinate for faithful 1:1 control parity. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="label2"
                   Canvas.Left="487"
                   Canvas.Top="-28"
                   FontSize="21"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                   Text="" />

        <!-- panel1: WinForms Panel @ (25,18) sized 779 x 242 (originally BackColor AliceBlue). Used
             purely as a grouping container; left transparent so the themed window frame shows through
             (AliceBlue and the form's LightCyan were all-but-identical light tints). Its children are
             positioned in the panel's own coordinate space via the nested Canvas, matching the
             WinForms panel-relative Locations exactly. -->
        <Border x:Name="panel1"
                Canvas.Left="25"
                Canvas.Top="18"
                Width="779"
                Height="242"
                Background="Transparent">
            <Canvas>

                <!-- ===================== LEFT column — Shutdown ===================== -->

                <!-- labelShutdown: caption above the shutdown button. WinForms @ (63,30), Tahoma 12 Bold.
                     Text "Shutdown" is the designer placeholder; code-behind sets gStr.gsShutdown. -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelShutdown"
                           Canvas.Left="63"
                           Canvas.Top="30"
                           FontSize="16"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           Text="Shutdown" />

                <!-- btnShutDown: WinForms Button @ (69,52) 79 x 79, BackgroundImage=Resources.SwitchOff,
                     Zoom. Powers off the computer (btnShutDown_Click ⇒ DialogResult.Yes). -->
                <Button x:Name="btnShutDown"
                        Classes="imageButton"
                        Canvas.Left="69"
                        Canvas.Top="52"
                        Width="79"
                        Height="79"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Shutdown"
                        Click="btnShutDown_Click">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SwitchOff.png"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- labelShutdownIn: WinForms Label @ (31,145), Tahoma 15.75 Bold. Part of the Shutdown
                     countdown pair — collapsed by default (shown only when setWindow_isShutdownComputer).
                     Text set at runtime to gStr.gsShutdownIn + ":". -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelShutdownIn"
                           Canvas.Left="31"
                           Canvas.Top="145"
                           FontSize="21"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           IsVisible="False"
                           Text="Shutdown In:" />

                <!-- lblShutCtr: WinForms Label @ (65,175), Tahoma 36 Bold — the large shutdown countdown
                     number. Collapsed by default; code-behind sets the value each tick. -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="lblShutCtr"
                           Canvas.Left="65"
                           Canvas.Top="175"
                           FontSize="48"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           IsVisible="False"
                           Text="10" />

                <!-- ===================== CENTER column — Cancel ===================== -->

                <!-- labelCancel: caption above the cancel/return button. WinForms @ (340,30), Tahoma 12
                     Bold. Text set at runtime to gStr.gsCancel. -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelCancel"
                           Canvas.Left="340"
                           Canvas.Top="30"
                           FontSize="16"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           Text="Cancel" />

                <!-- btnReturn: WinForms Button @ (321,43) 101 x 96, BackgroundImage=Resources.back_button,
                     Zoom. Abandons the exit and returns to AgOpenGPS (btnReturn_Click ⇒ DialogResult.Ignore). -->
                <Button x:Name="btnReturn"
                        Classes="imageButton"
                        Canvas.Left="321"
                        Canvas.Top="43"
                        Width="101"
                        Height="96"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel"
                        Click="btnReturn_Click">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/back-button.png"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- ====================== RIGHT column — Exit ====================== -->

                <!-- labelExit: caption above the exit button. WinForms @ (620,30), Tahoma 12 Bold,
                     TextAlign TopCenter (moot under AutoSize). Text set at runtime to gStr.gsExit. -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelExit"
                           Canvas.Left="620"
                           Canvas.Top="30"
                           FontSize="16"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           Text="Exit" />

                <!-- btnOk: WinForms Button @ (595,52) 90 x 79, BackgroundImage=Resources.WindowClose,
                     Zoom. Exits to Windows / closes AgOpenGPS (btnOk_Click ⇒ DialogResult.OK). -->
                <Button x:Name="btnOk"
                        Classes="imageButton"
                        Canvas.Left="595"
                        Canvas.Top="52"
                        Width="90"
                        Height="79"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Exit to Windows"
                        Click="btnOk_Click">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/WindowClose.png"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- labelExitToWindows: WinForms Label @ (542,145), Tahoma 15.75 Bold, TextAlign TopCenter
                     (moot under AutoSize). Part of the Exit countdown pair — visible by default. Text set
                     at runtime to gStr.gsExitToWindows + ":". -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelExitToWindows"
                           Canvas.Left="542"
                           Canvas.Top="145"
                           FontSize="21"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           IsVisible="True"
                           Text="Exit To Windows In:" />

                <!-- lblExitCtr: WinForms Label @ (612,175), Tahoma 36 Bold — the large exit countdown
                     number. Visible by default; code-behind sets the value each tick. -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="lblExitCtr"
                           Canvas.Left="612"
                           Canvas.Top="175"
                           FontSize="48"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                           IsVisible="True"
                           Text="3" />

            </Canvas>
        </Border>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
